    <string name="privacy_body">All recognition and automation run on this device. Camera frames, microphone audio, and drawn gestures are never uploaded or shared; data stays on your device. The accessibility service is used only to simulate gestures under your control.</string>
    <string name="disclosure_title">Before you start</string>
    <string name="disclosure_body">Phone Interaction uses the Android Accessibility Service to perform the taps and swipes you record. This is the only way Android lets an app simulate touch.\n\nWhat it does:\nRuns the actions you created, and only when you press Run or when a gesture or voice rule you set up is triggered.\nCan be stopped at any time: in the app, from the floating panel by tapping the screen, or from the notification.\n\nWhat it does NOT do:\nDoes not read your screen content, passwords or messages.\nDoes not collect, store or upload any personal data. Everything stays on your device, and the app has no internet access.\n\nYou can turn the service off at any time in Android Settings, Accessibility.</string>
