    <string name="a11y_restricted_title">Is the switch greyed out?</string>
    <string name="a11y_restricted_body">On Android 13 and newer, apps that were not installed from an app store are blocked by the system\'s \"Restricted settings\", which greys out the Accessibility switch.\n\nTo unlock it:\n1. Open App info\n2. Tap the menu in the top right corner\n3. Choose \"Allow restricted settings\"\n4. Come back to Accessibility and turn on Phone Interaction.\n\nIf that menu item is missing, this limitation is not active on your device.</string>
